From bd31c665623f59a4e5756abc60c0f413d2792d8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 04:32:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: R13B's two b10819 repair commits become
 also_commits of the mechanisms they keep alive

`protected-win validate --ref lane-210/offrig-union-2026-09-06` refused on two
rows: 6ef196cd1 (six merge-defect repairs) and 697027562 (tq_rotate joins
y_needs_reformat). Both carry a `Measured-effect:` trailer whose content is a
build/test outcome, so the strict discovery predicate reads them as unregistered
wins. R17 left them as R13B's to close (owed #6).

The gate offers two routes and this commit takes the third one the gate already
reads. The baseline ledger is CLOSED by mechanism to post-tip shas, so no
disposition can be written there. Registering a repair as its own win would be
an invented entry - neither commit adds a mechanism; each keeps a registered one
compiling or correct on the new base. `also_commits` is a field
`covered_win_commits` already consults (arifi_sync.py:1362), so attaching the
repairs to the entries they repair is a disposition the gate understands without
being weakened:

  - 697027562 -> vulkan-tq-matvec-subgroup (ggml-vulkan.cpp is its protected
    path; tq_rotate is the activation-rotate staging its mat-vec consumes)
  - 6ef196cd1 -> vulkan-tq-matvec-subgroup (defect 2, same file) AND
    powerinfer-pipeline-init-reuse (defect 1, src/llama-context.cpp, its
    protected path). One sha, two homes, because one repair touched two
    registered mechanisms.

Each entry carries an `_also_commits_note` stating exactly this, so the gate's
silence on those two shas is explained in the register, not bought. R13B/HQ may
re-home them.

validate: FAIL (2 problems) -> PASS, 22 entries, 40 paths, 43 anchors.

WI: WI-1698
Lane: lane-210
